# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-installed-subprocess-binary-not-discovered — find the distributed clautolisp engine
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-installed-subprocess-binary-not-discovered
#+DATE: 2026-10-06

* Context

The installed Clautolisp distribution deliberately separates dispatch
launchers from implementation-specific saved images:

#+begin_example
PREFIX/bin/alfe
PREFIX/bin/clautolisp
PREFIX/libexec/clautolisp/binaries/OS/CPU/alfe-sbcl[.exe]
PREFIX/libexec/clautolisp/binaries/OS/CPU/clautolisp-sbcl[.exe]
#+end_example

The two saved images are not interchangeable.  In particular,
=clautolisp-sbcl= contains runtime subsystems which the smaller =alfe-sbcl=
image does not embed.  The subprocess backend exists precisely to run that
complete standalone engine.

* Reproduction

Install a release under a non-standard prefix and run the installed alfe
without adding its implementation-specific =libexec= directory to =PATH=:

#+begin_src sh
PREFIX=/opt/clautolisp
PATH="$PREFIX/bin:$PATH" \
  "$PREFIX/bin/alfe" --clautolisp --backend subprocess --host cador \
  --dwg drawing.dwg --quit
#+end_src

The same defect was observed in SCHME GitLab job 527207.  Its installation
lived under =$CI_PROJECT_DIR/.clautolisp=, but detection failed with:

#+begin_example
alfe: alfe CLAUTOLISP backend error (phase DETECT):
clautolisp-sbcl not found (looked in
.../.clautolisp-build-527207/autolisp-front-end/source/../../clautolisp/tools/clautolisp/bin/clautolisp-sbcl,
/usr/local/bin/clautolisp-sbcl) [NO-SUBPROCESS-BINARY]
#+end_example

The binary was present at:

#+begin_example
$CI_PROJECT_DIR/.clautolisp/libexec/clautolisp/binaries/linux/x86-64/clautolisp-sbcl
#+end_example

On the Windows server the corresponding installed file is:

#+begin_example
C:/RunForestRun/outils/local/libexec/clautolisp/binaries/windows/x86-64/clautolisp-sbcl.exe
#+end_example

* Cause

=candidate-clautolisp-binaries= currently tries only:

1. =$ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN=;
2. the source-checkout path captured while compiling alfe;
3. =clautolisp-sbcl= on =PATH=;
4. =/usr/local/bin/clautolisp-sbcl=.

After packaging, the captured checkout path is stale and the build directory
may already have been deleted.  The installed =bin= directory contains the
portable dispatchers, not a =clautolisp-sbcl= image.  Detection never derives
the installation prefix from the running alfe program and therefore never
examines the canonical distributed =libexec= location.

This makes an installation incomplete from alfe's point of view even though
all advertised files were installed correctly.

* Temporary downstream workaround

SCHME derives the installed prefix from the =clautolisp= dispatcher, maps the
native OS and CPU to the distribution directory names, appends =.exe= only on
Windows, and passes the resulting absolute pathname through
=ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN=.  This downstream knowledge must be removed once alfe
performs the same discovery itself.

* Required fix

1. Determine the installation prefix of the running alfe image or launcher
   without depending on the current directory or the vanished build tree.
2. Add the canonical candidate
   =PREFIX/libexec/clautolisp/binaries/OS/CPU/clautolisp-sbcl[.exe]= before
   generic =PATH= and =/usr/local/bin= fallbacks.
3. Use the same OS, architecture and executable-suffix normalization as the
   release dispatchers; do not maintain a second incompatible mapping.
4. Preserve =$ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN= as the highest-priority explicit override.
5. Report every installed-layout candidate in the =NO-SUBPROCESS-BINARY=
   diagnostic when discovery fails.
6. Document that an installed alfe automatically finds the clautolisp engine
   shipped in the same prefix.

* Acceptance criteria

- A release installed under an arbitrary prefix runs
  =alfe --clautolisp --backend subprocess= without =PATH= entries for
  =libexec= and without =$ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN=.
- The test passes on Linux and Windows, including the required =.exe= suffix
  on Windows and its absence on POSIX.
- The installation prefix may contain spaces and may be moved after staging;
  discovery remains relative to the running installation.
- Running from an unrelated current directory does not affect discovery.
- A stale compile-time checkout path cannot shadow or invalidate the shipped
  engine.
- An explicit =$ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN= still wins and is covered by a regression
  test.
- Packaged-release verification launches the installed =alfe= subprocess
  backend against the installed =clautolisp-sbcl= image, rather than testing
  only source-tree binaries.
- The alfe user manual, specifications and man page describe the installed
  discovery order.

* Resolution (2026-10-06, alfe 2.2.157)

=candidate-clautolisp-binaries= (autolisp-front-end/source/backend-clautolisp.lisp)
now tries, in order:

1. =$ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN= (non-empty);
2. =installed-clautolisp-binaries=: the =clautolisp-sbcl[.exe]= in the
   directory of the RUNNING alfe executable (its truename, via
   =alfe.backend.cad-common:*executable-pathname-function*=, the same
   source the installed runtime assets use), then
   =PREFIX/libexec/clautolisp/binaries/OS/CPU/clautolisp-sbcl[.exe]= for
   every prefix =installation-prefixes= derives from it (deepest
   =libexec= ancestor, or =bin/= parent). Only an alfe executable claims
   an installation (not a dev image running as sbcl/ccl);
3. the compile-time checkout path, only when that file exists;
4. =$PATH= (split on =;= on Windows, =:= elsewhere; the walk looks for
   the platform name, =.exe= on Windows);
5. =/usr/local/bin/clautolisp-sbcl= (not on Windows).

The sibling candidate needs no OS/CPU mapping at all: the dispatcher
already chose the directory and EXECs the image from it, so discovery
works when =alfe-sbcl= is run through =PREFIX/bin/alfe= and when it is
run directly from =libexec=. For the =PREFIX/bin= layout the libexec
candidate names OS/CPU with =distribution-os-name= /
=distribution-arch-name=, documented as the same mapping as
=dispatch.sh= / =dispatch.cmd= / the top Makefile's REL_OS/REL_ARCH /
drawing-dwg's =%os= / =%arch=. The dispatcher was not changed (no
exported prefix variable was needed).

=NO-SUBPROCESS-BINARY= now lists every candidate tried and names
=$ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN= as the remedy. backend-clautolisp now depends on
backend-cad-common (which exports =alfe-executable-p=).

Tests (backend-clautolisp-tests.lisp, injected executable/OS/CPU/env/PATH):
installed Linux x86-64 (no suffix, prefix with spaces), PREFIX/bin layout
adds the libexec candidate (darwin/arm64), Windows x86-64 (=.exe=, no
/usr/local/bin), dev image claims nothing, stale checkout ignored when
absent and ranked after the installed engine when present,
=$ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN= wins, PATH separator per platform, diagnostic lists
candidates, and an end-to-end DETECT against a pretend installation under
a prefix with a space. alfe SBCL suite: 1511 checks, 0 failures.

Installed-layout simulation (built alfe-sbcl + clautolisp-sbcl copied to
=TMP/pre fix/libexec/clautolisp/binaries/linux/x86-64/=, checkout engine
hidden, cwd unrelated, PATH=/usr/bin:/bin, no ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN):
=alfe-sbcl --clautolisp --backend subprocess --host cador -x '(princ 42)' --quit=
printed 42, exit 0, both run directly and through =PREFIX/bin/alfe=
(dispatch.sh); with the engine removed it exited 3 listing
=TMP/pre fix/libexec/.../clautolisp-sbcl= and =/usr/local/bin/clautolisp-sbcl=.

Not covered here: a native Windows run (the Windows candidate is unit
tested from Linux with an injected executable), and a packaged-release
CI verification lane launching the installed alfe subprocess backend
(acceptance item; would belong to the release pipeline).
